From 0837f4e5909b435e1a873f7cd57b657276a117ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:46:03 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: add the SIMD&FP registers and basic Advanced SIMD
 instructions

The SIMD&FP registers V0 to V31 become the vector registers of the
architecture, modelled as 128-bit words. The calling convention passes
vector arguments in V0 to V7 and results in V0 to V3, and declares V8 to
V15 callee-saved. The procedure call standard only requires the low 64
bits of V8 to V15 to be preserved; the compiler saves and restores all 128.

New instructions, with a V prefix where the assembly mnemonic is also a
general-purpose one: MOV (vector), LDR and STR of a Q register, AND, BIC,
ORR, EOR, NOT, ADD, SUB, SHL, USHR, SRI and SLI. The element size of the
arrangement is the suffix of the intrinsic: VADD_4u32 is ADD Vd.4S. A
memory-argument condition restricts the address of a Q-register load or
store to the encodable forms, and immediate conditions restrict the shift
amounts to the range of each instruction. All of them are listed as
data-independent-time instructions.

Lowering maps u128 moves, loads and stores, the bitwise operators and the
element-wise additions, subtractions and shifts by a constant to these
instructions. Linearization saves and restores vector registers with
STR and LDR of a Q register.
